package flareite:extension@2.0.0;

/// The language servers the extension declares, which Flareite
/// runs: their arguments and settings, as the extension's settings or the
/// open folder call for. Needs the `language_servers` permission. The
/// manifest's `args` and `settings` apply until these change them, and
/// last until the extension stops; the user's `[lsp.servers.<name>]`
/// settings go over both.
///
/// A server declared by an extension with code starts after the extension
/// has activated, if it activates for one of the server's languages (or
/// on startup), so `activate` can configure it first.
interface language-servers {
  use types.{api-error};

  /// Replaces the arguments of one of its servers (by name). An argument
  /// may name a file on the web as `${download:https://...}`: Flareite
  /// downloads it, keeps it (getting it again once it's a day old), and
  /// puts its path in its place; an argument whose file can't be had is
  /// left out. Running instances of the server restart if the arguments
  /// changed. At most 32 arguments of 1,000 characters each.
  set-arguments: func(server: string, args: list<string>) -> result<_, api-error>;

  /// Replaces the settings of one of its servers: a JSON object, which
  /// answers the server's `workspace/configuration` requests (dotted keys,
  /// like `"a.b"`, are nested objects). Running instances are told with
  /// `workspace/didChangeConfiguration`. At most 256 KiB.
  set-settings: func(server: string, settings: string) -> result<_, api-error>;

  /// Restarts the running instances of one of its servers, as a setting
  /// it reads only at startup needs.
  restart: func(server: string) -> result<_, api-error>;
}
